{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind Adventure in Japan**\n\nLast month, I spent two weeks in Japan, and every moment was pure magic. My journey began in Tokyo, where neon lights and towering skyscrapers set the pace. Exploring Shinjuku’s bustling streets, I marveled at the contrast between sleek technology and deep-rooted traditions. A stop at Tsukiji Market revealed the freshest sushi I’ve ever tasted—meltingly tender tuna straight from the ocean.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took the shinkansen (bullet train) to Kyoto, where ancient temples and serene gardens awaited. Strolling through Arashiyama’s bamboo forest felt like stepping into a dream, the light filtering through the towering stalks creating an otherworldly glow. At Fushimi Inari, thousands of red torii gates led up the mountain, each one whispering stories of the past.\n\nNext, I ventured to Osaka, where street food stalls in Dotonbori dazzled with creativity. Takoyaki (octopus balls) and okonomiyaki (savory pancakes) became daily staples. The lively energy of Osaka’s nightlife was infectious, blending fun with heartfelt connections.\n\nMy final stop was Hiroshima, a place of profound history and resilience. Visiting the Peace Memorial Park reminded me of the power of hope and the importance of peace.\n\nJapan left me spellbound—its balance of tradition and innovation, efficiency and warmth, left an indelible mark. I can’t wait to return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.27843376994132996}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.037113383412361145}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.018043426796793938}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -4.7801782784517854e-05}, {"token": " Adventure", "logprob": -0.8805687427520752}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.08243269473314285}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.005001414567232132}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -0.110663577914